00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:40.132
Our Supreme Court justice

00:16:42.301 --> 00:16:44.670
took just one generation of segregation.

00:16:45.437 --> 00:16:47.373
The Supreme Court

00:16:47.906 --> 00:16:50.175
of the United States

00:16:53.145 --> 00:16:55.848
As I told folks at the time.

00:16:57.483 --> 00:17:00.085
She's smarter than you are.

00:17:02.087 --> 00:17:02.588
As Dr.

00:17:02.588 --> 00:17:04.089
King said,

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.692
give us the ballot

00:17:06.892 --> 00:17:09.461
and we will place judges on the bench.

00:17:09.461 --> 00:17:11.563
Who will do justly

00:17:12.631 --> 00:17:14.366
And we are.

00:17:14.767 --> 00:17:17.603
That's the promise of America,

00:17:17.603 --> 00:17:19.671
where change is hard but necessary

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.508
excuse me.

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:25.677
Progress is never easy,

00:17:25.711 --> 00:17:28.080
but it's always possible

00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:31.216
The things do get better.

00:17:31.216 --> 00:17:34.887
And our marched toward
a more perfect union.

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:37.589
But at this inflection point,

00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:40.993
we know there's a lot of work
to ask to continue in economic justice.

00:17:42.127 --> 00:17:43.796
Civil rights.

00:17:43.796 --> 00:17:45.697
Voting rights.

00:17:45.798 --> 00:17:48.567
Protecting our democracy.

00:17:48.634 --> 00:17:50.636
And I'm remembering

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:52.871
that our job is to redeem

00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:56.241
the soul of America.

00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:56.909
Look,

00:18:02.614 --> 00:18:04.850
I get accused of being an inveterate

00:18:06.452 --> 00:18:07.820
optimist.

00:18:10.055 --> 00:18:12.825
I call that the Irish of it.

00:18:13.525 --> 00:18:15.194
We're never on top, always stepped on.

00:18:15.194 --> 00:18:17.596
But we were optimistic,

00:18:18.197 --> 00:18:18.730
like Dr.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.200
King was optimistic.

00:18:22.868 --> 00:18:23.969
Folks

00:18:25.871 --> 00:18:27.573
as I said,

00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:30.476
progress is never easy.

00:18:31.977 --> 00:18:32.478
Redeeming

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.480
the soul of the country
is absolutely essential.

00:18:36.115 --> 00:18:38.984
I doubt whether any of us
would have thought,

00:18:38.984 --> 00:18:39.651
even in Dr.

00:18:39.651 --> 00:18:41.186
King's time, that the literally

00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:43.922
the institutional structures
of this country might collapse

00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:48.660
like you're seen in Brazil

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.830
or seen in other parts of the world.

00:18:53.198 --> 00:18:54.166
Folks

00:18:55.167 --> 00:18:57.269
are closer. This

00:18:57.436 --> 00:18:59.004
with a blessing

00:18:59.271 --> 00:19:02.641
I see today in the Oval Office

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:04.510
and many of you been there.

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:05.677
Been there in my office.

00:19:06.678 --> 00:19:07.346
You get to set

00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:09.348
it up the way you want within reason.

00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:14.353
As I sit at my desk

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:21.226
as I sit at my desk

00:19:23.061 --> 00:19:25.898
and look at the fireplace,

00:19:25.898 --> 00:19:28.000
just to the left

00:19:28.634 --> 00:19:29.735
is the bust of Dr.

00:19:29.735 --> 00:19:30.469
King.

00:19:32.571 --> 00:19:35.407
Is there in that spot on purpose?

00:19:37.376 --> 00:19:41.213
Because he was my inspiration as a kid.

00:19:41.647 --> 00:19:43.882
He does know

00:19:45.217 --> 00:19:48.587
where we should go

00:19:48.887 --> 00:19:50.222
I ran for three reasons.

00:19:50.222 --> 00:19:52.491
I said I wanted to restore
the soul of America.

00:19:53.559 --> 00:19:56.695
I wanted to rebuild this country
from the bottom up, in the middle out.

00:19:58.096 --> 00:20:00.365
And I wanted to unite it

00:20:01.166 --> 00:20:03.802
and not far from him, if you look

00:20:03.802 --> 00:20:07.172
about 40, 50 degrees to the right.

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:10.275
There is another

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:11.577
statue

00:20:12.811 --> 00:20:14.413
another bust

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.482
of Rosa Parks.

00:20:19.484 --> 00:20:19.818
People

00:20:19.818 --> 00:20:25.824
ask me why

00:20:28.026 --> 00:20:31.530
I say I put in my words,
she just say, I've had enough

00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:36.568
I've had enough.

00:20:38.704 --> 00:20:39.871
Folks.

00:20:40.172 --> 00:20:42.241
I often think of the question that Dr.

00:20:42.241 --> 00:20:45.744
King asked us all those years ago.

00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:48.113
I think it's important
you all remember but this is important.

00:20:48.146 --> 00:20:50.048
The nation remember it,

00:20:50.449 --> 00:20:51.783
he said.

00:20:52.284 --> 00:20:54.920
Where do we go from here?

00:20:56.221 --> 00:20:59.958
That's a quote Where do we go from here?

00:21:02.894 --> 00:21:03.762
Well, my message

00:21:03.762 --> 00:21:06.398
to the nation on this day
is we go forward.

00:21:07.699 --> 00:21:09.868
We go together

00:21:10.402 --> 00:21:11.670
when we choose democracy.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:15.841
Over autocracy,
a beloved community over chaos.

00:21:16.241 --> 00:21:18.810
We choose believers in the dreams

00:21:19.945 --> 00:21:21.480
to be doers.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.482
To be unafraid.

00:21:23.482 --> 00:21:25.917
Always keeping the faith.

00:21:25.917 --> 00:21:28.687
Every time I walk out of my Irish-Catholic
grandfather's

00:21:28.687 --> 00:21:31.523
home up in Scranton, Pennsylvania,
his name was Ambrose Finnegan.

00:21:32.891 --> 00:21:35.794
And Joe Joey, keep the faith.

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:38.797
My grandmother. No, Joey.

00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:40.465
Spread it.

00:21:40.465 --> 00:21:43.035
Spread the faith. Now, I'm serious.

00:21:46.838 --> 00:21:47.939
It's a Catholic grocery.

00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:49.474
I have my wrist.

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:52.077
One my son had on a day night.
He was dying.

00:21:52.411 --> 00:21:54.646
The point is, there's hope.

00:21:55.514 --> 00:21:57.749
There's always hope.

00:21:57.749 --> 00:21:59.851
We have to believe in.

00:21:59.851 --> 00:22:01.753
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:22:03.121 --> 00:22:03.789
that was Dr.

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:07.292
King's path, in my view,
path of keeping the faith

00:22:09.528 --> 00:22:11.630
It must be our path.

00:22:12.297 --> 00:22:16.368
Folks, for God's sake,
this is the United States of America.

00:22:17.069 --> 00:22:18.070
The United States.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.305
There's nothing beyond our capacity.

00:22:20.305 --> 00:22:22.274
Nothing beyond our capacity.

00:22:22.274 --> 00:22:24.509
If we set our mind to it.

00:22:24.509 --> 00:22:28.780
And ladies and gentlemen, we're
a land of dreamers and a land of doers.

00:22:29.614 --> 00:22:33.118
Nothing is beyond our capacity
in the gospel song that Dr.

00:22:33.118 --> 00:22:36.588
King loved,
as I understand he's always told, he did.

00:22:37.789 --> 00:22:40.559
We've come too far from where we started.

00:22:41.426 --> 00:22:43.562
Nobody told me that
the road would be easy.

00:22:44.396 --> 00:22:47.065
I don't believe he brought
me this far to leave me.

00:22:48.233 --> 00:22:50.569
He did not care this far to leave me.

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:55.907
My fellow Americans, I don't think
the Lord brought us this far to leave us.

00:22:56.174 --> 00:22:57.576
I really don't.

00:22:57.576 --> 00:22:59.778
My word lady.

00:22:59.911 --> 00:23:02.447
My fellow Americans.

00:23:02.914 --> 00:23:04.216
God bless Dr.

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:06.752
Martin Luther King and his family.

00:23:06.752 --> 00:23:12.157
And based on his one of his favorite
hymns, Precious Lord, take my hand

00:23:12.691 --> 00:23:17.095
through the storm, through the night
and lead me on to the light.

00:23:17.562 --> 00:23:18.864
May God bless you all.

00:23:18.864 --> 00:23:20.432
Let's go find the light.

00:23:20.432 --> 00:23:22.401
We can do this.

00:23:22.667 --> 00:23:23.435
I hate

00:23:24.369 --> 00:23:27.839
to do

